# shiso-local-logit-vectors-v1
# label capture-skeleton
# captured_from none
# The capture request the committed golden was filled from. Kept beside it so a
# recapture asks for exactly the same five frontiers rather than approximately
# them, and so a reviewer can see what was asked for without reading 320 recorded
# logits to infer it.
#
# Every frontier is the whole of its prompt, so each recorded top-1 is a real
# continuation that a person can read and judge rather than the model's guess at
# the middle of a sentence.
#
# The two long cases are the point of the file. The three short ones fit inside a
# single prefill call; a three-thousand-token frontier is what crosses the
# chunk boundary and reaches the wide attention and recurrent paths, which is
# where a port's launch geometry goes wrong.
# case <id> <mode> <ctx> <frontier> <prompt-file> <top-count>
case short_italian_fact text 1024 15 ../prompts/short_italian_fact.txt 64
case short_reasoning_plain text 1024 18 ../prompts/short_reasoning_plain.txt 64
case short_code_completion text 1024 23 ../prompts/short_code_completion.txt 64
case long_memory_archive text 4096 3493 ../prompts/long_memory_archive.txt 64
case long_code_audit text 4096 3957 ../prompts/long_code_audit.txt 64
